eat":9.7,"trend":"down","trendPct":-16.4,"badges":[],"participantCount":2,"sourceCount":2,"sourceNames":["Phys.org","Nature"],"participants":[{"iconUrl":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/10e9894789c239cf80ae91e9309b86733b3184b34dc245d1434d4eb8ab8ebd56.webp","iconSrcSet":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/274bcdc98d04a2b209beed660f59fbbf4cac33b3ef34c691ccadb9559d46572e.webp 48w, /hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/10e9894789c239cf80ae91e9309b86733b3184b34dc245d1434d4eb8ab8ebd56.webp 96w","name":"Nature","kind":"editorial"},{"iconUrl":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/0d041b355a9843928c182efcae3dde7fefee4b2e0224795801d24676153cf0a8.webp","iconSrcSet":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/3d9f1092de237734c1d9b47f5f7f2e9fceaf7f66932ef9d5bb357a8c16037d89.webp 48w, /hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/0d041b355a9843928c182efcae3dde7fefee4b2e0224795801d24676153cf0a8.webp 96w","name":"Phys.org","kind":"editorial"}],"spark":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,5.5,5.3,5.1,14.8,14.4,14,13.6,13.2,12.8,null,12.1,11.8,11.4,11.1,null,10.5,null,9.9],"summary":"JGU与MPI-BP联合团队在《Nature》发表研究，首次通过荧光探针在活细胞中观测到核孔内蛋白动态呈流体状，并揭示糖基化与转运受体进口素β蛋白共同维持屏障流动性，运输主要沿孔缘进行。该成果为理解细胞核物质交换机制及神经退行性疾病提供了新证据。研究结合活细胞成像、分子动力学模拟和冷冻电镜技术，发现柔性蛋白链的流动性受糖基化程度与进口素β蛋白浓度梯度双重调控，且该特性在多种真核生物中均被验证。","latest":"JGU与MPI-BP联合团队在《Nature》发表核孔内流体状屏障动态研究","cover":null},{"rank":3,"story":{"publicId":"b5108806-72e6-46d1-9fe0-545843aae461","title":"Nature研究证实极端干旱致美洲993种仙人掌栖息地丧失超80%"},"heat":8.5,"trend":"down","trendPct":-15.8,"badges":[],"participantCount":2,"sourceCount":2,"sourceNames":["Phys.org","Nature"],"participants":[{"iconUrl":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/10e9894789c239cf80ae91e9309b86733b3184b34dc245d1434d4eb8ab8ebd56.webp","iconSrcSet":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/274bcdc98d04a2b209beed660f59fbbf4cac33b3ef34c691ccadb9559d46572e.webp 48w, /hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/10e9894789c239cf80ae91e9309b86733b3184b34dc245d1434d4eb8ab8ebd56.webp 96w","name":"Nature","kind":"editorial"},{"iconUrl":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/0d041b355a9843928c182efcae3dde7fefee4b2e0224795801d24676153cf0a8.webp","iconSrcSet":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/3d9f1092de237734c1d9b47f5f7f2e9fceaf7f66932ef9d5bb357a8c16037d89.webp 48w, /hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/0d041b355a9843928c182efcae3dde7fefee4b2e0224795801d24676153cf0a8.webp 96w","name":"Phys.org","kind":"editorial"}],"spark":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,14.1,13.7,13.3,12.9,12.6,12.2,11.9,11.5,11.2,null,10.6,10.3,10,9.7,null,9.1,null,8.6],"summary":"《自然》论文通过整合iNaturalist 300万份观测数据与全球干旱预测模型（2000-2023年），首次在气候模型中纳入极端干旱事件，发现美洲993种仙人掌因干旱失去至少80%适宜栖息地，其中智利、秘鲁等热点地区损失最严重。研究指出传统气候模型忽略极端干旱，导致物种损失预测被低估。该结论已通过同行评审（2026-11-12发表），直接支持IUCN对部分仙人掌物种的濒危等级调整，并警示栖息地破坏与非法采集叠加将加剧灭绝风险。","latest":"某研究团队在 Nature 发表全球气候变暖威胁仙人掌物种的论文","cover":null}]}